{"base_rate":0.3844121532364597,"brier":0.1520443857331572,"bss":0.35748504343465626,"bss_hi":0.43794399866785944,"bss_lo":0.2658184260061071,"chart":{"base":[560.5,57.6],"fp":[270.7,305.7],"lead":"62,267.4 272,247.7 482,209.4 692,149.5","note":{"base":"skill 0.36 — higher than 67% of cities","fp":"low end +7pp, high end +14pp","lead":"day-1 error 1.0 °C — better than 77% of cities","rel":"promised 1% → rained 8%; promised 99% → rained 83%"},"rel":"67.2,429.6 220.6,344.2 520.1,198.3 688.3,108.7"},"country":"SE","deep":false,"depth":["Rain-probability calibration","Calibration curve","Seasonal split"],"ece":0.09453104359313078,"ess":379.6967180083942,"html":{"answer":"\n<h2 id=\"answer\">The short answer for Vaesteras</h2>\n<div class=\"verdict\">\n<p class=\"lead\"><b>The Vaesteras rain forecast is genuinely useful, though 4 points on its probability scale are off by more than chance explains.</b></p>\n<p>When it says rain is <i>near certain</i> (99%), believe about\n<b>83%</b>. When it says rain is <i>very unlikely</i>\n(0%), there is still roughly a <b>7%</b> chance.</p>\n<p class=\"muted\">Based on 757 days, 2024-04-26 to\n2026-05-31. \"Rain\" means at least 0.2 mm measured at\nVASTERAS-HASSLO, 5.2 km from the forecast grid point.\nSkill score 0.36, ranked 70 of\n213 &mdash; but see the rank <i>range</i>\n(41&ndash;115) before reading anything into\nthat position.</p>\n</div>\n\n<h3>What the percentages actually mean here</h3>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th class=\"num\">It said</th><th class=\"num\">It rained</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Days</th><th>Verdict</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class='num'>0%</td><td class='num'><b>7%</b></td><td class='num'>223</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>3%</td><td class='num'><b>14%</b></td><td class='num'>74</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">underpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>15%</td><td class='num'><b>14%</b></td><td class='num'>73</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>34%</td><td class='num'><b>41%</b></td><td class='num'>83</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>62%</td><td class='num'><b>55%</b></td><td class='num'>75</td><td><span class=\"tag good\">honest</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>85%</td><td class='num'><b>70%</b></td><td class='num'>67</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr><tr><td class='num'>99%</td><td class='num'><b>83%</b></td><td class='num'>162</td><td><span class=\"tag bad\">overpromised</span></td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">4 of 7 groups are further from honest than chance\nalone can explain. The rest are indistinguishable from a perfect forecast.</p>\n","card":"\n<div class=\"gcard\">\n  <p class=\"gcard-head\"><b>Vaesteras</b> <span class=\"muted\">Sweden</span></p>\n  <p class=\"gcard-tier\"><span class=\"tag good\">Genuinely useful</span>\n    <span class=\"muted\">4 points off by more than chance</span></p>\n  <dl class=\"gcard-stats\">\n    <div><dt>Skill score</dt><dd>0.36</dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Rank</dt><dd>41&ndash;115\n      <span class=\"muted\">of 213</span></dd></div>\n    <div><dt>Record</dt><dd>757 <span class=\"muted\">days</span></dd></div>\n  </dl>\n  <p class=\"gcard-more\"><a href=\"#answer\">The full verdict for\n    Vaesteras &darr;</a></p>\n</div>","curve":"\n<h2 id=\"curve\">The calibration curve</h2>\n<p>Each dot is a group of days sharing a similar forecast. Horizontal position\nis what was promised; vertical is what happened. <b>On the dashed diagonal =\nhonest.</b> Hover any dot for its sample size.</p>\n<figure><svg viewBox=\"0 0 430 430\" width=\"100%\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Calibration curve for Vaesteras\"><rect class=\"chart-plot\" x=\"58\" y=\"18\" width=\"354\" height=\"364\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"58\" y2=\"18\"/><line class=\"chart-grid\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"382\"/><text class=