917808219 69.33756756756758,382.0 58.0952466367713,382.0\" opacity=\"0.16\"/><line class=\"chart-ideal\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"382\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"18\" stroke-dasharray=\"5,4\" stroke-width=\"1.3\"/><line class=\"chart-base\" x1=\"58\" y1=\"242.07397622192866\" x2=\"412\" y2=\"242.07397622192866\" stroke-dasharray=\"2,3\"/><polyline class=\"chart-line\" points=\"58.0952466367713,357.5156950672646 69.33756756756758,332.81081081081084 111.19698630136986,332.13698630136986 178.65855421686746,232.89156626506025 276.11119999999994,183.01333333333335 359.4283582089552,126.65671641791045 409.9240740740741,80.91358024691357\" fill=\"none\" stroke-width=\"2.4\"/><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 0%&amp;#10;It rained 7% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 223 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"58.0952466367713\" cy=\"357.5156950672646\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 3%&amp;#10;It rained 14% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 74 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"69.33756756756758\" cy=\"332.81081081081084\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 15%&amp;#10;It rained 14% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 73 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"111.19698630136986\" cy=\"332.13698630136986\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 34%&amp;#10;It rained 41% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 83 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"178.65855421686746\" cy=\"232.89156626506025\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 62%&amp;#10;It rained 55% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 75 days&amp;#10;within the range a perfect forecast would give\"><circle class=\"chart-dot\" cx=\"276.11119999999994\" cy=\"183.01333333333335\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 85%&amp;#10;It rained 70% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 67 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"359.4283582089552\" cy=\"126.65671641791045\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><g class=\"pt\" data-tip=\"Forecast said 99%&amp;#10;It rained 83% of the time&amp;#10;Based on 162 days&amp;#10;outside the perfect-forecast range - real miscalibration\"><circle class=\"chart-dot sig\" cx=\"409.9240740740741\" cy=\"80.91358024691357\" r=\"6.5\" stroke-width=\"2\"/></g><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"235.0\" y=\"422\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\">What the forecast promised</text><text class=\"chart-label\" x=\"15\" y=\"200.0\" font-size=\"12.5\" text-anchor=\"middle\" transform=\"rotate(-90 15 200.0)\">How often it actually rained</text></svg>\n<figcaption>Green band = where a <b>flawless</b> forecast would still land, given\nhow few days we have. Red dots fall outside it, so those are real errors rather\nthan noise. The faint horizontal line is climatology\n(38%).</figcaption></figure>\n","season":"\n<h2 id=\"season\">Does the season matter?</h2>\n<p>In Vaesteras the forecast is most skilful in\n<b>spring</b> (0.45) and least in\n<b>summer</b> (0.19).</p>\n<div class=\"tablewrap\">\n<table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th class=\"num\">Days</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Rain days</th><th class=\"num\">Skill score</th>\n<th class=\"num\">Avg error</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>summer</td><td class='num'>184</td><td class='num'>46%</td><td class='num'>0.194</td><td class='num'>13.0%</td></tr><tr><td>autumn</td><td class='num'>180</td><td class='num'>37%</td><td class='num'>0.336</td><td class='num'>7.5%</td></tr><tr><td>winter</td><td class='num'>175</td><td class='num'>43%</td><td class='num'>0.406</td><td class='num'>10.7%</td></tr><tr><td>spring</td><td class='num'>218</td><td class='num'>30%</td><td class='num'>0.451</td><td class='num'>7.1%</td></tr></tbody></table>\n</div>\n<p class=\"muted\">Four-way splits of a two-year record are thin, so read the\nordering as indicative. Coarser binning is used here than for the annual curve\nfor the same reason.</p>\n"},"lat":59.61617,"lon":16.55276,"n":757,"n_cities":213,"name":"Vaesteras","offset_days":0,"pop_map":[{"hi":0.02,"lo":0.0,"mean":0.0002690582959641256,"n":223,"obs":0.06726457399103139,"sig":true},{"hi":0.08,"lo":0.02,"mean":0.03202702702702703,"n":74,"obs":0.13513513513513514,"sig":true},{"hi":0.25,"lo":0.08,"mean":0.15027397260273972,"n":73,"obs":0.136986301369863,"sig":false},{"hi":0.47,"lo":0.25,"mean":0.3408433734939759,"n":83,"obs":0.40963855421686746,"sig":false},{"hi":0.76,"lo":0.47,"mean":0.6161333333333332,"n":75,"obs":0.5466666666666666,"sig":false},{"hi":0.96,"lo":0.76,"mean":0.8514925373134329,"n":67,"obs":0.7014925373134329,"sig":true},{"hi":1.0,"lo":0.96,"mean":0.9941358024691359,"n":162,"obs":0.8271604938271605,"sig":true}],"prcp_km":5.2,"provisional":false,"rank":70,"rank_hi":115.02499999999998,"rank_lo":41.0,"reliability":0.011333475329552894,"resolution":0.09513467105202558,"skill_pct":null,"slug":"vaesteras","station":"VASTERAS-HASSLO","timezone":"Europe/Stockholm"}